  <link:footnoteLink xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/link" xlink:type="extended">
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-1" id="fn-1" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ANR Storage Company's contract quantity at 12/31/2025 was 57,494,520 Dth.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-2" id="fn-2" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Gas Withdrawn from Storage represents respondent's use of system gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The ANR Storage Company "Fuel and Line Loss Percentage" does not identify seperate fuel and loss components. All gas retained from shippers is reported as "Gas Received from Shippers as Compressor Station Fuel".</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Reciepts represents a decrease in customer inventory and storage adjustments.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Gas Delivered to Storage represents respondent's replacement of system gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Deliveries and Gas Used for Operations represents an increase in customer inventory, and gas used for other utility operations.</link:footnote>
